    "done_when": "watch.watch_text and watch.watch_document catch sqlite3.DatabaseError (which covers OperationalError) raised while opening or querying the index through TelemetryIndex.readonly; the text output then states that the index at its path could not be read and quotes the error text, printing no period or ledger rows, and the --json document's index block carries exists true, readable false and error set to the error text, with empty record, ledger and periods; a readable index's block carries readable true; TelemetryIndex.readonly takes a timeout keyword defaulting to 5.0 seconds and its docstring states that a read waits at most that long for the writer's lock and then raises, replacing the sentence saying a read never blocks behind the writer; tests in tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py assert, for a zero-byte index file, that both outputs report it unreadable with the text no such table and leave the file at zero bytes, and, for an index whose lock a second connection holds with BEGIN EXCLUSIVE, that the report names database is locked, the test passing a short timeout rather than waiting five seconds; gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py tests/test_agent_watch_live.py tests/test_agent_watch_cost.py tests/test_telemetry_index.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status",
